WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.192 --> 00:00:02.568
- Korea is a highly competitive workplace.

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.365
It's super competitive for students.

00:00:04.365 --> 00:00:06.628
- You have to have perfect
grades, the perfect looks.

00:00:06.628 --> 00:00:09.314
- Everyone there talks
about beauty constantly,

00:00:09.314 --> 00:00:12.222
and they tell you straight to
your face that you're ugly,

00:00:12.222 --> 00:00:13.806
or that you should get plastic surgery.

00:00:13.806 --> 00:00:16.236
- That's why people feel like it's a good

00:00:16.236 --> 00:00:18.438
career move to get plastic surgery.

00:00:18.438 --> 00:00:20.597
- What we're doing today
is sort of recreating

00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:23.078
this practice that's very common in Korea,

00:00:23.078 --> 00:00:24.679
but in a way that's not permanent.

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:28.315
Really, a sort of sliding
door's potential second reality

00:00:28.315 --> 00:00:31.648
if I had chosen to alter the way I look.

00:00:35.027 --> 00:00:38.251
- So, I am a quarter Korean
and I lived in the south

00:00:38.251 --> 00:00:41.295
of South Korea in a city
called Daegu for a year,

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:43.564
and I saw a lot of shit when I was there.

00:00:43.564 --> 00:00:47.117
All of the subways are
plastered with banner ads

00:00:47.117 --> 00:00:49.826
that say you should get plastic surgery.

00:00:49.826 --> 00:00:52.292
I actually had an article
that I wrote about on BuzzFeed

00:00:52.292 --> 00:00:54.489
that also went viral on The Daily Mail

00:00:54.489 --> 00:00:56.046
where the headline was literally

00:00:56.046 --> 00:00:58.445
"Too fat, too tall, and too dark

00:00:58.445 --> 00:01:00.041
"To be beautiful in South Korea."

00:01:00.041 --> 00:01:01.820
and that's honestly how I felt.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.146
- When I was a kid I felt
like my eyes were small

00:01:05.146 --> 00:01:07.432
because I didn't have double eyelids.

00:01:07.432 --> 00:01:09.416
I had a couple of relatives suggest

00:01:09.416 --> 00:01:11.716
that I get a double eyelid surgery.

00:01:11.716 --> 00:01:13.943
In some ways, I think
about it, and I'm like,

00:01:13.943 --> 00:01:14.776
"That's messed up."

00:01:14.776 --> 00:01:17.993
In other ways it was an
act of concern and love.

00:01:17.993 --> 00:01:20.938
- To grow up in a society
and a culture that's very

00:01:20.938 --> 00:01:25.870
frank about the way you look,
changes the way you perceive

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.141
your personal relationship with beauty.

00:01:28.141 --> 00:01:30.841
First time I went to Korea,
all of my mom's friends there

00:01:30.841 --> 00:01:32.845
looked at me right when
I got off and they said,

00:01:32.845 --> 00:01:36.230
"Well, your son could get the
eye surgery, and a nose job,

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:37.696
"And get his face smaller."

00:01:37.696 --> 00:01:39.126
I had a lot of insecurities about that.

00:01:39.126 --> 00:01:40.887
I thought, "Oh, maybe
it's because I am ugly.

00:01:40.887 --> 00:01:43.193
"Maybe it's because they want
me to look a certain way."

00:01:43.193 --> 00:01:46.228
Fast forward to now when my
mom, to the same friends,

00:01:46.228 --> 00:01:48.563
shows videos of me and they all say,

00:01:48.563 --> 00:01:50.836
"Oh, your son is so handsome.

00:01:50.836 --> 00:01:52.853
"Oh, there's nothing wrong with his face."

00:01:52.853 --> 00:01:55.098
Do you know why the fuck
they changed their minds?

00:01:55.098 --> 00:01:56.395
Because I'm successful now.

00:01:56.395 --> 00:01:58.662
So, if you think about
it, a lot of Koreans

00:01:58.662 --> 00:02:01.241
don't necessarily say you
will look better because

00:02:01.241 --> 00:02:04.461
you're white-looking, they're
thinking you can survive

00:02:04.461 --> 00:02:06.868
and succeed more if you
change certain things

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.823
because that is what's
happening in society.

00:02:08.823 --> 00:02:10.678
- I'm really terrified
of what this surgeon

00:02:10.678 --> 00:02:12.138
